      "title": "Misrepresentation and false advertising",
      "narration": "Misrepresentation is giving a false or misleading account of a policy: its benefits, exclusions, premiums, dividends or the insurer’s financial condition. False advertising is the same deception in a brochure, website, seminar or ad. Telling Priya that a plan covers all prescriptions when it has a formulary, or calling a hospital indemnity policy health insurance, misrepresents. Omitting a material limitation can mislead as surely as a false statement. Maryland treats both as unfair trade practices under Section 27-202, with penalties, restitution and license discipline. The cure is the same standard from Lesson 10: say what the policy does, what it does not, and who stands behind it.",
