      "narration": "Competition is lawful; lying about competitors is not. Defamation under Section 27-204 is making or circulating a false or maliciously critical statement about an insurer’s financial condition that is calculated to injure its business. Theo may point out that a rival plan has a narrower network; he may not claim the rival is insolvent without basis. Section 27-205 prohibits knowingly false statements about an insurer’s financial condition and false or deceptive entries in insurer records, including altering records to mislead an examiner. Fabricating a client’s signature on an application or backdating a receipt falls here as well as under fraud.",
