      "title": "Rebating",
      "narration": "A rebate is anything of value given to induce a purchase that is not specified in the policy: returning part of the commission, paying the first premium, giving a gift card after the sale. Section 27-209 prohibits rebating and inducements. Maryland allows educational materials, promotional materials and merchandise costing no more than 50 dollars, but receipt may not be conditioned on buying insurance. A 20 dollar notebook handed to everyone at a seminar is lawful; the same notebook promised only to those who enroll is a rebate. Both parts of the exception, the dollar limit and the no-condition rule, must be met. Rebating is a violation for the producer and for a client who knowingly accepts it.",
