      "title": "Twisting",
      "narration": "Twisting is inducing a policyholder to lapse, surrender, replace, convert or retain a policy through misrepresentation or an incomplete comparison. Section 27-213 covers retention as well as replacement: telling Rosa her current insurer is failing to make her switch is twisting, and so is falsely telling her the new plan is worse to keep her from switching. An honest, complete comparison that leads to a replacement is lawful, as Lesson 14 explained. The difference lies in the accuracy and completeness of what the producer says. Medigap and long-term care replacement rules add their own notices on top of the general prohibition.",
